course: dictionary
lesson: 14741
title: Who receives the promise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A promise always has two people in it. The one who makes the promise is the promisor. The one the promise is made to, and who will receive what was promised, is the promisee. «Mia promised her little brother a bike ride.» Mia is the promisor, and her brother is the promisee.
explain: The ending -ee often shows the person who receives something, as in employee or payee. A promisee is the person who receives the promise, so the word fits that pattern. Think: the promisee is the one who gets the promise kept.
explain: You will mostly meet this word in law books, where it is used in contracts, which are written agreements. In everyday talk, you can just say «the person you promised». Knowing the word helps you spot who is owed something when you read about a promise.
fact: A promisee is the person to whom a promise is made.
fact: The promisee is the one who will receive what was promised.
fact: The person who makes the promise is called the promisor.
fact: «Promisee» is a noun, and its plural is promisees.
fact: It is a rare, formal word, used mostly in law.
exercise: «Sam promised Ali he would share his crisps.» Who is the promisee? | Crisps | *Ali | Sam | Nobody
exercise: In a promise, what is the person who makes it called? | Promisee | Promiser's friend | Promisal | *Promisor
exercise: Which word means the person a promise is made to? | *Promisee | Promise | Promised | Promisor
test: «The school promised the class a trip to the zoo.» In this sentence, who is the promisor? | The trip | The zoo | The class | *The school
test: In a written agreement, who is the promisee? | The person who makes the promise | *The person the promise is made to | A person who keeps the promise | The lawyer who writes the agreement
exam: «Ruth promised Tom a birthday cake.» Tom is the | Promise | Cake | Promisor | *Promisee
